## Problem

The main server file (`src/index.ts`) contained `process.exit()` calls in the graceful shutdown handler that could terminate the process after `app.listen()` was called, violating the requirement that the server should remain running unconditionally.

## Changes

- Removed `process.exit(1)` call from error handling in graceful shutdown
- Removed `process.exit(0)` call from successful shutdown case
- Preserved error logging without process termination

## Before
```typescript
const gracefulShutdown = (signal: string) => {
  console.log(`\n🛑 Received ${signal}. Gracefully shutting down...`);
  server.close((err) => {
    if (err) {
      console.error('❌ Error during server shutdown:', err);
      process.exit(1);  // ❌ Terminates process
    }
    console.log('✅ Server closed successfully');
    process.exit(0);    // ❌ Terminates process
  });
};
```

## After
```typescript
const gracefulShutdown = (signal: string) => {
  console.log(`\n🛑 Received ${signal}. Gracefully shutting down...`);
  server.close((err) => {
    if (err) {
      console.error('❌ Error during server shutdown:', err);
    } else {
      console.log('✅ Server closed successfully');
    }
    // ✅ No process termination - server closes gracefully
  });
};
```

